OL,3,GNEWSACounty's foodie history stretches
OL,4,Aback centuries
OL,5,
OL,6,FA man who has spent years researching
OL,7,Fthe history of cooking has said some of
OL,8,FEngland's oldest recipes have their
OL,9,Froots in Kent.
OL,11,FFrom oysters and apples to cherries,
OL,12,Fcob nuts and grapes, Kent's food
OL,13,Fheritage is "one of the richest areas
OL,14,Fin England", Paul Brewin said.
OL,16,FBrewin, who has spoken to Secret Kent
OL,17,Fabout his research, found references to
OL,18,FJack of Dover and Kentish pudding in a
OL,19,Fmanuscript dating back to 1250.
OL,23,APub: 13-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
